  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The automatic recorder no longer needs Numpad9 and still performs no camera or input writes. One measurement gap remained: it first sampled after the state edge, so it had no true pre-change rendered position, rotation, FOV, or look baseline. It now preserves the prior eligible rendered frame and emits that baseline before the transition samples. This gives the later curve repair a real starting point instead of a guessed one. Source and focused camera checks pass, but this change is not built or installed; the final shared-curve repair still waits for the automatic runtime sample.",
